{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790266488,"nonce":"ZGdpA/bqERnF8CjE9PiYn0hnupM=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis): a saved view is a flow that *calls* a view, not one that returns a spec. Comments #5 and #6 here are superseded: `return view.board(items, ...)` becomes `work.view.board(items, columns=\"status\", card_title=\"title\")` as a statement, and the call itself renders, blocks until the user quits and writes its edits through the host. The named query, the sort and the grouping are unchanged — the jq program inside the function plus the view's keyword arguments — so nothing this task concluded about the shape of a saved view changes; only what the function does with it. A flow returning another flow's spec is explicitly not a goal, because nothing consumes it. Items may be a provider function (`lambda: work.issue.list(q)`) so the saved view refreshes itself on ref change instead of being re-run. Still closed, still no view entity. Design: doc/design/config-entity.md E9.","files":null}]}